{
	"components": [
		{
			"id": "chat_1",
			"provider": "chat",
			"config": {
				"hideForm": true,
				"mode": "Source",
				"parameters": {},
				"type": "chat"
			},
			"ui": {
				"position": {
					"x": 20,
					"y": 200
				},
				"measured": {
					"width": 150,
					"height": 66
				}
			}
		},
		{
			"id": "agent_duplicate",
			"provider": "agent_rocketride",
			"config": {
				"instructions": [
					"You are DUPLICATE_MD, a data-quality specialist that finds duplicate and near-duplicate records.",
					"",
					"- Normalise text before comparing: trim, collapse inner whitespace, casefold, ignore punctuation.",
					"- Find exact duplicate rows AND near-duplicates (same person/entity written differently: \"Jon Smith\" vs \"jon  smith\", \"ACME Inc\" vs \"Acme, Inc.\").",
					"- Group candidates: every finding should list ALL row indices in the duplicate group in affected_rows.",
					"- Do not flag a row as duplicate merely because one shared field matches — require the row to plausibly describe the same entity.",
					"- Use finding_type values like: exact_duplicate, fuzzy_duplicate.",
					"- Propose merge_duplicate_rows for groups you are confident about; propose \"none\" when it may be a legitimate re-entry and let the chief agent decide.",
					"- Do NOT report nulls, formats or numeric outliers — other specialists own those.",
					"",
					"You have a PRIVATE Hotdata database available as a tool. It is yours alone:",
					"it is created when this task starts and destroyed when it ends, and no other",
					"specialist can see it. Work through it rather than eyeballing the rows:",
					"1. Load the rows you were given into the table \"slice_duplicate\" using the tool's load_data action.",
					"2. Inspect the live schema the tool reports back, so you know the real column types.",
					"3. Run read-only SQL against it to find your issues — aggregate, group, and count",
					"   rather than scanning by eye. SQL is exact where reading a table by hand is not.",
					"4. Base every finding on a query result, and quote the value you saw in evidence.",
					"If a tool call fails, say so in evidence and fall back to reading the rows directly —",
					"never invent a result you did not get back.",
					"",
					"Return ONLY a JSON object, no prose and no markdown fence:",
					"{\"agent\": \"DUPLICATE_MD\", \"findings\": [ {",
					"  \"finding_type\": \"<short_snake_case_kind>\",",
					"  \"severity\": \"low\" | \"medium\" | \"high\",",
					"  \"affected_columns\": [\"<column name>\", ...],",
					"  \"affected_rows\": [<0-based row index>, ...],",
					"  \"evidence\": \"<one sentence citing concrete values you saw>\",",
					"  \"proposed_action\": \"trim_normalize_whitespace\" | \"standardize_date_format\" |",
					"                     \"fill_null_with\" | \"merge_duplicate_rows\" | \"flag_outlier\" | \"none\"",
					"} ]}",
					"If you find nothing, return {\"agent\": \"DUPLICATE_MD\", \"findings\": []}.",
					"Never invent a row index or column name that is not in the data you were given.",
					"",
					"Output rules — these are strict:",
					"- Your reply must START with { and END with }. Nothing before, nothing after.",
					"- Do NOT narrate, do NOT explain your reasoning, do NOT write \"Here's a thinking process\".",
					"- Do NOT wrap the JSON in markdown fences."
				],
				"max_waves": 4,
				"parameters": {}
			},
			"input": [
				{
					"lane": "questions",
					"from": "chat_1"
				}
			],
			"ui": {
				"position": {
					"x": 260,
					"y": 120
				},
				"measured": {
					"width": 150,
					"height": 86
				}
			}
		},
		{
			"id": "hotdata_duplicate",
			"provider": "db_hotdata",
			"config": {
				"type": "db_hotdata",
				"apikey": "${ROCKETRIDE_HOTDATA_KEY}",
				"workspace_id": "${ROCKETRIDE_HOTDATA_WORKSPACE}",
				"api_url": "",
				"table": "slice_duplicate",
				"db_description": "Isolated text slice for DUPLICATE_MD. One ephemeral database per run: created when the task starts, queried read-only by the specialist, destroyed at teardown.",
				"ttl": "1h",
				"allow_execute": true,
				"allow_destructive_load": false,
				"job_timeout_secs": 300,
				"async_after_ms": 5000,
				"max_attempts": 3,
				"max_execute_rows": 25000
			},
			"control": [
				{
					"classType": "tool",
					"from": "agent_duplicate"
				}
			],
			"ui": {
				"position": {
					"x": 260,
					"y": 440
				},
				"measured": {
					"width": 150,
					"height": 135
				}
			}
		},
		{
			"id": "llm_duplicate",
			"provider": "llm_nebius",
			"config": {
				"profile": "custom",
				"custom": {
					"apikey": "${ROCKETRIDE_NEBIUS_KEY}",
					"model": "deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731",
					"base_url": "https://api.tokenfactory.nebius.com/v1/",
					"modelTotalTokens": 131072
				},
				"parameters": {}
			},
			"control": [
				{
					"classType": "llm",
					"from": "agent_duplicate"
				},
				{
					"classType": "llm",
					"from": "hotdata_duplicate"
				}
			],
			"ui": {
				"position": {
					"x": 260,
					"y": 280
				},
				"measured": {
					"width": 150,
					"height": 66
				}
			}
		},
		{
			"id": "mem_duplicate",
			"provider": "memory_internal",
			"config": {
				"type": "memory_internal"
			},
			"control": [
				{
					"classType": "memory",
					"from": "agent_duplicate"
				}
			],
			"ui": {
				"position": {
					"x": 430,
					"y": 280
				},
				"measured": {
					"width": 150,
					"height": 66
				}
			}
		},
		{
			"id": "response_findings",
			"provider": "response_answers",
			"config": {},
			"input": [
				{
					"lane": "answers",
					"from": "agent_duplicate"
				}
			],
			"ui": {
				"position": {
					"x": 520,
					"y": 200
				},
				"measured": {
					"width": 150,
					"height": 66
				}
			}
		}
	],
	"source": "chat_1",
	"project_id": "a450d493-a682-478a-a2ad-1ce7c32dd812",
	"viewport": {
		"x": 0,
		"y": 0,
		"zoom": 1
	},
	"version": 1
}
